  "name": "track plan: a scissors crossover with parallel routes, in Auto",
  "covers": [
    "Track plan: a scissors crossover with parallel routes"
  ],
  "about": "Each route takes everything from its signal to the end of the drawing. A train along the north line and one along the south line take only their own lines' pieces of the scissors, so both signals clear together. Leaving at the far end, neither asks for the signal it came past: each came from the scissors. Later both crossovers are set: the two diagonal routes clash only on the crossing. The train that asked first takes it; the other waits, and goes once the crossing is freed behind the first train, while the first still holds the south line's piece it is in. Each turnout of the first route unlocks as its piece is freed behind the train.",
